  "summary": "## Spotify Toolkit\n\nThe Spotify toolkit connects Arcade to the Spotify API, enabling LLM-powered control of playback, search, and catalog lookup on a user's Spotify account.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- **Playback control** — pause, resume, skip to next/previous track, and seek to an absolute or relative position within the current track (position clamped automatically to valid boundaries).\n- **Playback state & devices** — retrieve what is currently playing (track or episode, progress, play/pause state, active device) and list all available devices.\n- **Track play & queueing** — play a track by name, play a list of tracks, or play an artist (auto-queues four additional tracks by the same artist).\n- **Catalog search** — search Spotify with field filters (`album`, `artist`, `track`, `year`, `genre`, `isrc`, `upc`, `tag:new`, `tag:hipster`) scoped to relevant result types; supports year ranges and combined filter expressions (e.g., `remaster track:Doxy artist:Miles Davis`).\n- **Track metadata** — fetch detailed information about a specific track.\n\n## OAuth\n\nThis toolkit uses **OAuth 2.0** via Spotify. See the [Arcade Spotify auth provider docs](https://docs.arcade.dev/en/references/auth-providers/spotify) for setup details."
}